---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Type shadowing errors\n;\n; Tests that defining a type that shadows a builtin or parent module type\n; produces a compile-time error.\n\n; ============ Shadowing a builtin type ============\n\nMODULE Builtins {\n  ; Error: `Int` shadows a builtin type\n  NEWTYPE Int = String\n}\n\n; ============ Shadowing a parent module type ============\n\nMODULE Parent {\n  +NEWTYPE Id = Int\n\n  MODULE Child {\n    ; Error: `Id` already in scope from outer module\n    NEWTYPE Id = String\n  }\n}\n\n; ============ Shadowing deeply nested ============\n\nMODULE Deep {\n  +TYPE Status = Active | Inactive\n\n  MODULE Level1 {\n    MODULE Level2 {\n      ; Error: `Status` already in scope from outer module (Deep)\n      TYPE Status = On | Off\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
---
ERROR: type `Int` shadows a builtin type
type `Id` already in scope from outer module
type `Status` already in scope from outer module
